1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,693
TEO (V.O.): What does a man look like... when

2
00:00:02,393 --> 00:00:04,051
TEO (V.O.): he succeeds completely at

3
00:00:03,751 --> 00:00:05,844
TEO (V.O.): everything his world asks of him?

4
00:00:06,544 --> 00:00:07,552
NOA: Okay.

5
00:00:07,512 --> 00:00:09,124
NOA: Hear me out.

6
00:00:09,084 --> 00:00:11,753
NOA: David, then Solomon, then Jesus.

7
00:00:11,713 --> 00:00:12,953
NOA: It's one arc.

8
00:00:12,953 --> 00:00:15,381
NOA: David's the emotional, musical one.

9
00:00:15,341 --> 00:00:17,789
NOA: Chill... unless he's defending somebody.

10
00:00:18,089 --> 00:00:19,755
TEO: Your arc holds together.

11
00:00:19,715 --> 00:00:22,331
TEO: Honestly, better than you think.

12
00:00:22,531 --> 00:00:24,325
TEO: But one piece needs an

13
00:00:24,025 --> 00:00:25,956
TEO: honest correction first.

14
00:00:26,056 --> 00:00:27,308
NOA: Which piece?

15
00:00:27,408 --> 00:00:29,778
TEO: Chill unless defending.

16
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:32,706
TEO: The record is much more violent than that.

17
00:00:32,906 --> 00:00:34,748
TEO: And including the violence

18
00:00:34,448 --> 00:00:36,172
TEO: makes your arc stronger.

19
00:00:36,132 --> 00:00:37,237
TEO: Not weaker.

20
00:00:37,637 --> 00:00:38,471
NOA: Show me.

21
00:00:39,371 --> 00:00:41,244
TEO (V.O.): You're right that he was gifted.

22
00:00:41,204 --> 00:00:43,903
TEO (V.O.): He played music for a troubled king.

23
00:00:44,003 --> 00:00:46,468
TEO (V.O.): He loved his friend Jonathan with a

24
00:00:46,168 --> 00:00:48,076
TEO (V.O.): bond deeper than brothers.

25
00:00:48,176 --> 00:00:49,962
DAVID: I will dance before the Lord!

26
00:00:49,922 --> 00:00:51,444
DAVID: I will become even more

27
00:00:51,144 --> 00:00:52,614
DAVID: undignified than this!

28
00:00:52,714 --> 00:00:54,906
TEO (V.O.): He danced with everything he had.

29
00:00:54,866 --> 00:00:55,875
TEO (V.O.): And he wept.

30
00:00:55,835 --> 00:00:56,750
TEO (V.O.): Openly.

31
00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:57,879
TEO (V.O.): Without shame.

32
00:00:58,079 --> 00:00:59,626
DAVID: How long, O Lord?

33
00:00:59,586 --> 00:01:01,287
DAVID: Will you forget me forever?

34
00:01:01,787 --> 00:01:04,378
WOMEN: Saul has struck down his thousands...

35
00:01:04,078 --> 00:01:06,173
WOMEN: and David, his ten thousands!

36
00:01:06,373 --> 00:01:09,254
TEO (V.O.): His society rewarded him for killing.

37
00:01:09,214 --> 00:01:11,790
TEO (V.O.): And they sang about it in the streets.

38
00:01:12,390 --> 00:01:14,564
TEO (V.O.): Living among the Philistines,

39
00:01:14,264 --> 00:01:17,795
TEO (V.O.): he raided towns... and left no man or woman alive.

40
00:01:18,095 --> 00:01:19,851
TEO (V.O.): So that no survivor could

41
00:01:19,551 --> 00:01:21,248
TEO (V.O.): report what he had done.

42
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:24,967
TEO (V.O.): He took Bathsheba, the wife of Uriah,

43
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:27,090
TEO (V.O.): one of his own loyal soldiers.

44
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:28,712
DAVID: Set Uriah in the front of

45
00:01:28,412 --> 00:01:29,653
DAVID: the hardest fighting.

46
00:01:29,613 --> 00:01:31,183
DAVID: Then draw back from him,

47
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:32,559
DAVID: so that he is struck down.

48
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:35,097
TEO (V.O.): Uriah carried the letter himself.

49
00:01:35,057 --> 00:01:37,902
TEO (V.O.): His own death, sealed, in his hand.

50
00:01:38,902 --> 00:01:41,897
TEO (V.O.): Over an insult, he set out to kill

51
00:01:41,597 --> 00:01:44,672
TEO (V.O.): Nabal, and every male in his house.

52
00:01:44,772 --> 00:01:46,254
ABIGAIL: My lord, please.

53
00:01:46,214 --> 00:01:47,805
ABIGAIL: Do not carry the guilt of

54
00:01:47,505 --> 00:01:49,303
ABIGAIL: shedding blood without cause.

55
00:01:49,703 --> 00:01:51,141
DAVID: Blessed be your wisdom.

56
00:01:51,101 --> 00:01:53,162
DAVID: You kept me this day from bloodguilt.

57
00:01:53,262 --> 00:01:55,157
TEO (V.O.): He stopped only because a

58
00:01:54,857 --> 00:01:56,687
TEO (V.O.): woman stood in the road.

59
00:01:57,387 --> 00:01:58,396
DAVID: My son.

60
00:01:58,356 --> 00:02:00,587
DAVID: I wanted to build a house for God.

61
00:02:00,687 --> 00:02:03,286
DAVID: But God said to me: you shall not build it...

62
00:02:02,986 --> 00:02:04,971
DAVID: because you have shed much blood.

63
00:02:05,771 --> 00:02:06,621
DAVID: Joab.

64
00:02:06,581 --> 00:02:08,195
DAVID: Do not let his gray head go

65
00:02:07,895 --> 00:02:09,509
DAVID: down to the grave in peace.

66
00:02:09,709 --> 00:02:11,496
DAVID: And Shimei... bring his gray

67
00:02:11,196 --> 00:02:12,612
DAVID: head down with blood.

68
00:02:12,912 --> 00:02:15,292
TEO (V.O.): Even dying, the sword was the

69
00:02:14,992 --> 00:02:17,371
TEO (V.O.): last thing he handed his son.

70
00:02:18,371 --> 00:02:20,494
NOA: So... he wasn't chill.

71
00:02:20,694 --> 00:02:23,599
TEO: He did exactly what his society told him.

72
00:02:23,559 --> 00:02:25,478
TEO: And he was excellent at it.

73
00:02:25,578 --> 00:02:27,700
TEO: What it told him included killing.

74
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:29,093
TEO: And people cheered.

75
00:02:29,593 --> 00:02:32,220
NOA: So David is what it looks like... when

76
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:34,119
NOA: someone wins the whole program.

77
00:02:34,319 --> 00:02:35,238
TEO: Completely.

78
00:02:35,198 --> 00:02:36,975
TEO: And then... there's the kid who

79
00:02:36,675 --> 00:02:38,118
TEO: grew up inside that win.

80
00:02:38,918 --> 00:02:41,254
TEO (V.O.): Solomon was born to Bathsheba

81
00:02:40,954 --> 00:02:42,869
TEO (V.O.): after Uriah was killed.

82
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:44,876
TEO (V.O.): Their first child had died.

83
00:02:45,076 --> 00:02:47,463
TEO (V.O.): He grew up in a house where his brother

84
00:02:47,163 --> 00:02:49,015
TEO (V.O.): Amnon raped his sister Tamar.

85
00:02:49,215 --> 00:02:51,569
TEO (V.O.): Where Absalom killed Amnon for it.

86
00:02:51,529 --> 00:02:53,369
TEO (V.O.): Then rebelled against their

87
00:02:53,069 --> 00:02:55,252
TEO (V.O.): father... and died in the revolt.

88
00:02:55,352 --> 00:02:56,792
DAVID: O my son Absalom!

89
00:02:56,752 --> 00:02:58,394
DAVID: My son, my son!

90
00:02:58,354 --> 00:03:00,665
DAVID: If only I had died instead of you!

91
00:03:00,965 --> 00:03:02,899
TEO (V.O.): On the surface: a palace.

92
00:03:02,859 --> 00:03:04,188
TEO (V.O.): A beloved king.

93
00:03:04,148 --> 00:03:05,013
TEO (V.O.): Wealth.

94
00:03:04,973 --> 00:03:06,130
TEO (V.O.): God's favor.

95
00:03:06,130 --> 00:03:08,353
TEO (V.O.): Underneath: a father brilliant in

96
00:03:08,053 --> 00:03:10,218
TEO (V.O.): public... who could not stop the

97
00:03:09,918 --> 00:03:12,083
TEO (V.O.): destruction inside his own home.

98
00:03:12,383 --> 00:03:13,896
YOUNG SOLOMON: Something's wrong here.

99
00:03:13,856 --> 00:03:15,591
YOUNG SOLOMON: And nobody will say what it is.

100
00:03:16,191 --> 00:03:18,333
TEO (V.O.): Then Solomon got everything.

101
00:03:18,293 --> 00:03:20,670
TEO (V.O.): At a scale nobody else ever got.

102
00:03:20,670 --> 00:03:21,654
TEO (V.O.): Wisdom.

103
00:03:21,614 --> 00:03:22,480
TEO (V.O.): Wealth.

104
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,540
TEO (V.O.): Buildings.

105
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,405
TEO (V.O.): Gardens.

106
00:03:24,305 --> 00:03:26,198
TEO (V.O.): Seven hundred wives.

107
00:03:26,158 --> 00:03:28,387
TEO (V.O.): Three hundred concubines.

108
00:03:28,287 --> 00:03:29,280
TEO (V.O.): Forced labor.

109
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,993
TEO (V.O.): International fame.

110
00:03:31,093 --> 00:03:32,914
TEO (V.O.): If more were the answer,

111
00:03:32,614 --> 00:03:35,891
TEO (V.O.): he would have been the happiest man in history.

112
00:03:36,791 --> 00:03:38,622
SOLOMON: Vanity of vanities.

113
00:03:38,582 --> 00:03:39,749
SOLOMON: All is vanity.

114
00:03:40,049 --> 00:03:41,984
TEO (V.O.): The Hebrew word is hevel.

115
00:03:41,944 --> 00:03:42,795
TEO (V.O.): Vapor.

116
00:03:42,755 --> 00:03:43,510
TEO (V.O.): Breath.

117
00:03:43,470 --> 00:03:45,352
TEO (V.O.): Something you can't grab.

118
00:03:45,452 --> 00:03:47,101
SOLOMON: I made great works.

119
00:03:47,061 --> 00:03:48,395
SOLOMON: I built houses.

120
00:03:48,355 --> 00:03:50,342
SOLOMON: I planted vineyards for myself...

121
00:03:50,242 --> 00:03:52,293
SOLOMON: and behold, all was vanity,

122
00:03:51,993 --> 00:03:53,979
SOLOMON: and a striving after wind.

123
00:03:54,479 --> 00:03:55,768
SOLOMON: So I hated life.

124
00:03:56,068 --> 00:03:58,216
TEO (V.O.): Tradition says Solomon wrote it.

125
00:03:58,176 --> 00:04:00,054
TEO (V.O.): Many scholars think a later

126
00:03:59,754 --> 00:04:01,514
TEO (V.O.): writer took on his voice.

127
00:04:01,474 --> 00:04:03,775
TEO (V.O.): Either way... it's the report from the top.

128
00:04:04,675 --> 00:04:06,543
SOLOMON: There is one who has no other.

129
00:04:06,503 --> 00:04:07,521
SOLOMON: No son.

130
00:04:07,481 --> 00:04:08,559
SOLOMON: No brother.

131
00:04:08,519 --> 00:04:11,356
SOLOMON: Yet there is no end to all his toil... and his

132
00:04:11,056 --> 00:04:13,396
SOLOMON: eyes are never satisfied with riches.

133
00:04:13,896 --> 00:04:15,405
SOLOMON: Two are better than one.

134
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:16,746
SOLOMON: For if they fall,

135
00:04:16,446 --> 00:04:18,295
SOLOMON: one will lift up his fellow.

136
00:04:18,495 --> 00:04:21,233
SOLOMON: But woe to him who is alone when he falls,

137
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:23,265
SOLOMON: and has not another to lift him up.

138
00:04:23,465 --> 00:04:25,664
SOLOMON: If two lie together, they keep warm.

139
00:04:25,624 --> 00:04:27,588
SOLOMON: But how can one keep warm alone?

140
00:04:27,988 --> 00:04:30,420
SOLOMON: A threefold cord is not quickly broken.

141
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:33,450
NOA: That's... the door test.

142
00:04:33,550 --> 00:04:36,797
TEO: The man with everything says the emptiness is

143
00:04:36,497 --> 00:04:39,219
TEO: endless toil, with nobody beside you.

144
00:04:39,319 --> 00:04:41,891
TEO: Woe to him who is alone when he falls.

145
00:04:41,851 --> 00:04:43,931
TEO: That's the person on the floor...

146
00:04:43,631 --> 00:04:45,442
TEO: with zero doors to knock on.

147
00:04:46,042 --> 00:04:46,737
NOA: Yeah.

148
00:04:46,697 --> 00:04:48,123
NOA: I know that floor.

149
00:04:48,523 --> 00:04:50,063
TEO: I know you do.

150
00:04:50,463 --> 00:04:52,432
TEO: Now watch what the Son of

151
00:04:52,132 --> 00:04:54,100
TEO: David does with all this.

152
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:57,739
TEO (V.O.): They called Jesus the Son of David.

153
00:04:57,699 --> 00:05:00,241
TEO (V.O.): And he talked about Solomon directly.

154
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:02,503
JESUS: Consider the lilies of the field.

155
00:05:02,463 --> 00:05:04,541
JESUS: Even Solomon in all his glory was

156
00:05:04,241 --> 00:05:06,158
JESUS: not dressed like one of these.

157
00:05:06,358 --> 00:05:08,778
JESUS: Something greater than Solomon is here.

158
00:05:09,378 --> 00:05:12,089
TEO (V.O.): From David, he kept the heart.

159
00:05:12,049 --> 00:05:13,072
TEO (V.O.): The music.

160
00:05:13,032 --> 00:05:14,505
TEO (V.O.): The raw prayer.

161
00:05:14,465 --> 00:05:16,416
TEO (V.O.): The loyalty of a friend.

162
00:05:16,516 --> 00:05:18,307
PETER: Lord, should we strike with the sword?

163
00:05:18,507 --> 00:05:20,438
JESUS: Put your sword back in its place.

164
00:05:20,638 --> 00:05:21,929
JESUS: Love your enemies.

165
00:05:21,889 --> 00:05:23,821
JESUS: Pray for those who persecute you.

166
00:05:24,021 --> 00:05:26,862
TEO (V.O.): David's heart... with David's sword removed.

167
00:05:27,562 --> 00:05:30,856
TEO (V.O.): From Solomon, he took the proof.

168
00:05:30,816 --> 00:05:32,654
TEO (V.O.): That experiment had already

169
00:05:32,354 --> 00:05:34,020
TEO (V.O.): been run to the maximum.

170
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:36,340
JESUS: Do not store up treasures on earth.

171
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,690
JESUS: Go, sell what you have,

172
00:05:37,390 --> 00:05:38,733
JESUS: and come... follow me.

173
00:05:39,233 --> 00:05:40,473
TEO (V.O.): More wealth.

174
00:05:40,433 --> 00:05:41,848
TEO (V.O.): More buildings.

175
00:05:41,808 --> 00:05:43,030
TEO (V.O.): More achievement.

176
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:44,967
TEO (V.O.): It ended in 'I hated life.'

177
00:05:44,667 --> 00:05:46,210
TEO (V.O.): He didn't repeat it.

178
00:05:47,010 --> 00:05:50,235
TEO (V.O.): Instead of a palace, he built this.

179
00:05:50,195 --> 00:05:52,245
TEO (V.O.): Twelve people walking together.

180
00:05:52,205 --> 00:05:53,532
TEO (V.O.): Eating together.

181
00:05:53,492 --> 00:05:55,352
TEO (V.O.): Sleeping outside together.

182
00:05:55,452 --> 00:05:57,218
TEO (V.O.): Shared meals.

183
00:05:57,178 --> 00:05:58,699
TEO (V.O.): A shared purse.

184
00:05:58,659 --> 00:06:00,073
TEO (V.O.): Touching lepers.

185
00:06:00,033 --> 00:06:01,934
TEO (V.O.): Eating with outcasts.

186
00:06:01,934 --> 00:06:03,690
TEO (V.O.): A group where nobody was

187
00:06:03,390 --> 00:06:04,964
TEO (V.O.): alone when they fell.

188
00:06:05,264 --> 00:06:07,749
JESUS: Love one another, as I have loved you.

189
00:06:08,049 --> 00:06:10,082
JESUS: Where two or three are gathered in my

190
00:06:09,782 --> 00:06:11,394
JESUS: name, there I am among them.

191
00:06:11,594 --> 00:06:12,963
TEO (V.O.): Two. Three.

192
00:06:12,923 --> 00:06:14,406
TEO (V.O.): A threefold cord.

193
00:06:14,366 --> 00:06:15,996
TEO (V.O.): A village... embodied.

194
00:06:16,796 --> 00:06:18,965
NOA: A cord of three... instead of a crown.

195
00:06:19,165 --> 00:06:21,905
TEO: A table instead of a palace.

196
00:06:24,205 --> 00:06:25,004
AMI: Hey.

197
00:06:24,964 --> 00:06:26,321
AMI: I didn't call first.

198
00:06:26,281 --> 00:06:27,951
AMI: Is that okay?

199
00:06:28,351 --> 00:06:29,835
NOA: It's more than okay.

200
00:06:29,795 --> 00:06:30,594
NOA: Come in.

201
00:06:31,694 --> 00:06:33,259
TEO (V.O.): Two are better than one.

202
00:06:33,219 --> 00:06:35,122
TEO (V.O.): And a threefold cord... is

203
00:06:34,822 --> 00:06:36,293
TEO (V.O.): not quickly broken.
